# __NAME__ mcp

HTTP MCP server on `http://127.0.0.1:__PORT__/mcp`, generated by
mcp-orchestrator and managed from there.

## Adding a tool

Edit `__PACKAGE__/server.py`:

```python
@server.tool()
def __NAME___something(argument: str) -> dict:
    """One line on what this does, then when to use it."""
    return {"ok": True}
```

Then restart the server and the sessions that use it:

```
mcp_restart("__NAME__")          # new process, new tools
sessions_restart_pending(...)    # sessions pick them up at their next stop
```

The second step is not optional. Claude Code attaches MCP servers only at
process startup, so a running session keeps talking to the tool list it saw
when it launched.

## Running it by hand

```powershell
.\run.ps1
```

The orchestrator runs it hidden instead, so its output goes to the log:

```
mcp_logs("__NAME__")
```
